{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Elohim finished on the seventh day.</b> Rabbi Shimon says: Flesh and blood, who does not know his times and moments, must add from the profane onto the sacred. The Holy One, blessed be He, who knows His times and moments, entered it by a hair's breadth, and it appeared as though He finished in it, on that day. Another interpretation: What was the world lacking? Rest — the Sabbath came, rest came, the work was finished and completed."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:11.363534516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}